effort-optimizer

Based on effort-optimizer 0.1.0, the "benai-effort-optimizer" Claude Code mod by
Ben AI (https://www.benai.co). Redistributed in joel/skill-marketplace with the
author's permission.

Changes from 0.1.0 (in 0.2.0):
- The person's own effort setting is never written: every pick goes on the
  chat's requests for this session only (the turn.step rewrite upstream used
  as its fallback).
- The ~/.claude/mods/switches.json switch (benai's `mods` pane) is gone. The
  mod is turned off with `/plugin disable effort-optimizer`;
  `/effort-optimizer off|on` pauses it in the current chat only.
- Mode (suggest|auto) and the picker model live in userConfig, shown in
  /config; the commands and the dialog write the mode there.
- The home directory is read from HOME ($.env.get).
- The terminal gets its own Learn more wording and glyph, and band rows that
  fit its width.
- Each pick is shared in ~/.claude/mods-state/effort-<session>.json for
  helper-desk.
- The pure decisions moved to hooks/level.ts; tests were added (upstream had
  none).
Ben's four-question framework and its prompt are unchanged.
